= Game theory — Simple =

Game theory studies situations where what is best for one participant depends on what other participants do. Games can model competition, cooperation, bargaining, coordination, and conflict. A stable strategy pattern is not necessarily fair or best for the group.

'''Important boundary:''' game theory ≠ zero-sum games only.

